      "content": "thanks. i'll get the data ready. but before i do, i need to know if you can actually spot stuff that's meant to look \"normal\" but isn't. like, if someone is trying to trigger a psychological response or test my focus, they wouldn't send anything crazy, right? they'd just send things that look like standard pings but hit at specific intervals to see how i react. do you think it's possible to use mundane office communications to build a behavioral profile like that?",
